-- N2 example sentences, batch 2: scope, contrast, and the hypothetical.
--
-- に関して, に沿って, に反して, に限らず and に限り narrow or widen what a
-- statement covers. 〜反面 and 〜一方で set two halves of a thing against each
-- other. Then the ものなら pair, which look alike and mean opposite things:
-- potential + ものなら is a wish (帰れるものなら帰りたい), volitional +
-- ものなら is a threat (遅れようものなら叱られる) — so they are written back
-- to back. 〜といっても closes the batch by taking a claim back.
--
-- Nothing had to be reworded; all forty passed check:examples first time.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

